From: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
Date: Sat, 23 May 2026 19:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] bluestore: split read into bluestore_read/get_onode/_do_read
 sub-spans + accept parent trace

Once ceph-20.1.1-librados-read-trace.patch lands, RGW GETs propagate
OTel context to the OSD and op->osd_parent_span becomes a real
recording span on the read path. This patch threads that context
down through the read pipeline so BlueStore-level spans link under
the OSD's read trace instead of being orphan roots.

  * ObjectStore::read virtual gains an optional jspan_context*
    parent_trace param (defaults to nullptr; existing callers
    compile unchanged).
  * BlueStore::read and MemStore::read overrides updated.
  * BlueStore::read replaces the orphan start_trace from the
    bluestore-tracer-enable patch with a parent-aware span and adds
    two child spans:
      - get_onode: time spent loading the Onode from the kv store
      - _do_read: time spent in the actual extent read (BlueFS/bdev)
  * PGBackend::objects_read_sync and ReplicatedBackend's override
    take a parent jspan_ptr; pass its context to store->read.
  * PrimaryLogPG.cc updated at the four objects_read_sync call sites
    (CEPH_OSD_OP_READ, the chunk-read path, the dedup base read,
    and the direct hit-set-archive read) plus the direct store->read
    at the hit-set-archive site, to pass ctx->op->osd_parent_span's
    context.

After this, a GET trace fans out as:
  rgw_request → rados_read → op-request-created → dequeue_op → do_op
    → execute_ctx → bluestore_read → {get_onode, _do_read}

bluestore::tracer spans surface as service.name="bluestore" in Tempo,
and Prometheus span-metrics gain
traces_spanmetrics_latency_bucket{service="bluestore",
span_name="bluestore_read|get_onode|_do_read"} per OSD.

Signed-off-by: Chris Lu <lu@alcg.io>
